# Forbidden patterns

Reject these in review. Fix the model. Do not patch the result.

- Delay implemented as `t + k` or `readyAt`.
- Prefetch that predicts the next address, or an array that grows on every call. Depth stays 2.
- A second or third copy of the DRAM core.
- One global clock that steps SDR every tick.
- Float nanoseconds in the timebase.
- Hidden state inside a gate function.
- ACT on every request. A row hit skips ACT.
- One global queue that serializes every bank. Banks are an array of independent FSMs.
- RDRAM as a wide fast bus. ROW and COL headers must consume channel ticks.
- A full-duplex channel. One direction occupies the channel.
- Half-row slots that are occupied and never released on precharge or row change.
- Returning a hard-coded bandwidth or latency constant instead of running the tick loop.

```typescript
// BAD
if (arch === 'rdram') return { bandwidth: 1600, latency: 40 }

// GOOD
return runDevice(arch, requests)
```
